For every polarised part below, the per-part placement check states the
datasheet marking for pin 1 or the cathode, and the net that marked pad must
land on. Check that each makes electrical sense (a flyback diode's cathode on
the positive rail, an LED's anode towards the supply, a low-side MOSFET's
source on ground), and that the marking is a concrete physical feature, not
"see datasheet".

